Surface model (presentational parity, mirrors the web prop-driven component):
  The web CostPerKwhChart is a pure presentational child of the cost-analysis page: it takes a
  data: { date; costPerKwh }[] prop and renders either a recharts LineChart (data.length > 0) or a
  centered "Not enough data" empty state. It performs no fetching; the page owns the query lifecycle.
  The native surface follows the established presentational-leaf precedent (BatteryLevelChart, 0097): a
  ContentControl bound to a CostPerKwhChartModel (the web data prop + the parent's fetch flag),
  projected by the WinUI-free CostPerKwhChartProjection into a CostPerKwhChartDisplay. Never any HTTP.

Hooks bound (web -> native ; P1/S8 + P1/S9 + P1/S10):
  useTranslation  -> ILocalizer            (i18n facade ; English fallbacks asserted by PassthroughLocalizer)
  useChartPalette -> ChartPalette          (categorical brand brushes ; line = KeyForIndex(2) = web palette[2])
  useFormatting   -> ScalarFormatters.FormatCurrency   (the native formatCurrency ; 2-dp range summary)

Shared components (web -> native counterparts):
  @/components/ui     GlassPanel        -> TsGlassPanel (p-4 = Thickness 16) ; section title -> PanelTitle
  @/components/charts LineChart/Line/XAxis/YAxis/Tooltip -> TsLineChart (TsCartesianChart) + built-in
                      TsChartTooltip cursor ; empty -> TsEmptyState ; loading -> TsSkeleton
  (Per the established native charting precedent (SpeedTrendChart/SessionComparisonChart) the cartesian
   surface draws a numeric value axis; the web formatCurrency value-axis is reproduced for assistive
   technology via the currency-formatted range summary, see Accessibility.)

States (every branch renders a visible surface ; none hidden):
  [x] loading  parent fetch in flight -> title + TsSkeleton(260) ; LiveRegion announce
  [x] empty    web data.length === 0  -> title + TsEmptyState("Not enough data") (web h-[260px] box)
  [x] ready    web data.length > 0    -> title + TsLineChart (single $/kWh line, palette[2], 2-dp)
  error / stale / offline are owned by the data-fetching parent page, NOT this presentational leaf —
  exactly as the web source has only data/empty branches; rationale documented on CostPerKwhChartState
  (the same scoping the BatteryLevelChart precedent uses).

i18n keys (P1/S10 catalog Strings/en/Resources.resw ; exact web t() defaults ; no English literals in code):
  costAnalysis.charts.costPerKwh -> "Cost per kWh Trend"   (GlassPanel title)
  costAnalysis.charts.rateLabel  -> "$/kWh"                (Line series name)
  costAnalysis.charts.noData     -> "Not enough data"      (empty state)
  common.loading                 -> "Loading"              (loading branch)
  All four resolve through the facade; PassthroughLocalizer asserts the fallbacks row-for-row in tests.

Accessibility:
  Surface AutomationProperties.Name per state (title + loading / empty message / rate + currency range).
  Chart AutomationName = currency range summary ("$min-$max" via FormatCurrency, en-dash) — the spoken
  analogue of the web formatCurrency value axis. Decorative header icon = AccessibilityView.Raw.
  System font scale + theme (light/dark/high-contrast) honoured via tokens (no hard-coded hex).

Diagnostics (P1/S11):
